The `UnicodeDecodeError` is occurring because `QuerySet.delete()` (via `collector.collect`) forces the fetching of all fields for objects in the `QuerySet` (e.g., `SELECT * FROM ...`). When an object contains data that cannot be decoded by the current Python/DB adapter encoding (e.g., binary data or invalid characters in a text field), the hydration of the model instance fails.

Since `delete()` only needs the primary keys of the objects being deleted, we can optimize the `related_objects` method to use `.only('pk')` (or equivalent) to minimize the fields fetched, thus avoiding the issue.

